## Verification Reference

### Verification Objective

Demonstrate that the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) can acquire, maintain, and update observations of the operating environment in accordance with the requirements of SO-F-002.

---

### Verification Method

Verification of this objective shall be achieved through one or more of the following methods:

| Method | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| Analysis | Confirm that the perception architecture satisfies the objective. |
| Demonstration | Show that the system can perceive representative operating conditions. |
| Test | Verify that environmental observations are correctly acquired, maintained, and provided to downstream objectives. |

---

### Verification Reference

Detailed verification procedures shall be maintained within the AVIA Verification domain and referenced from this objective upon approval.

---

### Verification Success Criteria

Verification shall demonstrate that the system can:

- Acquire relevant environmental observations.
- Detect observable changes in operating conditions.
- Maintain an up-to-date observation state.
- Supply observations suitable for downstream interpretation.
- Operate within the engineering constraints defined by SO-F-002.

---

### Verification Status

Not Yet Verified

---

### Verification Notes

Verification shall evaluate the perception capability itself and shall not assess interpretation, reasoning, decision-making, or execution functions, which are addressed by subsequent Functional Objectives.
